.\" robodr-kafka-publish(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-export/src/bin/robodr-kafka-publish.rs and the crate README.
.\" Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-KAFKA\-PUBLISH 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-kafka\-publish \- publish RoboDR findings to the robot\-edr.findings Kafka topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-kafka\-publish
.B \-\-bootstrap
.I HOST:PORT
.RB [ \-\-bootstrap
.IR HOST:PORT ]...
.B \-\-state\-dir
.I DIR
.RB ( \-\-diode\-out
.I DIR
|
.B \-\-spool
.IR DIR )
.RB [ \-\-topic
.IR T ]
.RB [ \-\-chunk
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-client\-id
.IR S ]
.RB [ \-\-request\-timeout\-ms
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-delivery\-timeout\-ms
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-retries
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-request\-bytes
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-interval\-ms
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.RB [ \-\-upgrade\-data\-source
.IR LABEL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SOC\-side (high side) publisher. It reads either the
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1)
importer's
.IB DIR /<batch>/records.jsonl
.RB ( \-\-diode\-out )
or a connected site's
.BR robodr\-agentd (8)
spool
.RB ( \-\-spool ),
re\-validates every finding, requires its key and headers to be exactly those
derived from the value (contract \(sc2), computes the partition from the robot
id and the topic's current partition count (contract \(sc4) and produces the
record value byte for byte. An optional per\-finding signature header
.B robodr\-finding\-sig
(contract \(sc2a) must be the last header; it is shape\-checked and forwarded
verbatim, for the consumer to verify. Invalid or broker\-rejected records go to
a dead\-letter file; progress (committed line count per batch, done markers)
is replaced atomically after each acknowledged chunk.
.PP
Producer settings: acks=all, idempotence off (at\-least\-once delivery:
consumers drop duplicates on
.BR event\-uid ),
one request in flight, no compression.
.B No TLS or SASL:
run it on an isolated SOC network or through a local TLS proxy.
Verified against single\-node Apache Kafka 3.9.1 and 4.1.0 brokers
(\fBscripts/kafka\-it.sh\fR in the source tree). Pointed at a TLS or SASL
listener it fails with an error that says so.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-once
it publishes every
.B \-\-interval\-ms
and retries after an error; each step that published, dead\-lettered or
finished a batch prints a JSON report on stdout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-bootstrap " HOST:PORT"
Bootstrap broker (repeatable, at least one).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Progress, done markers and dead letters.
.TP
.BI \-\-diode\-out " DIR\fR | " \-\-spool " DIR"
The input (exactly one).
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " T"
Topic (default
.BR robodr.findings ).
.TP
.BI \-\-chunk " N"
Records per produce request (default 500).
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-id " S"
Kafka client id (default
.BR robodr\-kafka\-publish ).
.TP
.BI \-\-request\-timeout\-ms " N\fR, " \-\-delivery\-timeout\-ms " N"
Per\-request deadline (default 35000; it must exceed the broker\-side produce
timeout, 30000) and total delivery deadline per chunk
(default 120000).
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Retries of retriable errors (default 10, exponential backoff).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-request\-bytes " N"
Largest produce request (default 1 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-interval\-ms " N"
Loop interval, > 0 (default 2000).
.TP
.B \-\-once
One pass, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-upgrade\-data\-source " LABEL"
An unsigned contract 1.x record (written before an upgrade) is upgraded to
contract 2.0 with this
.B data_source
(default
.BR robodr )
and the publisher's topic, keeping its identity, and sent with headers derived
from the upgraded value. A signed 1.x record cannot be upgraded (its signature
covers the 1.x bytes) and is dead\-lettered with the reason
"legacy 1.x signed record: re\-sign required".
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.RB ( \-\-once ).
.TP
.B 1
Error with
.B \-\-once
(without it, errors are printed and retried).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SYSTEMD UNIT
The package ships
.B robodr\-kafka\-publish.service
(installed disabled) for a connected site: it runs on the unit or sensor box
as user
.B robodr
with
.B \-\-spool /var/lib/robodr/spool/agentd
and state in
.IR /var/lib/robodr/export/kafka\-publish ;
bootstrap brokers and extra flags come from
.I /etc/robodr/kafka\-publish.env
.RB ( ROBODR_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP ,
.BR ROBODR_KAFKA_PUBLISH_ARGS ).
The unit denies every IP address; the drop\-in example
.I 50\-brokers.conf.example
allows the brokers. List every broker of the cluster: the publisher connects
to the leader of each partition at its advertised address, not only to the
bootstrap broker. Use IP literals (and IP\-literal advertised listeners): DNS
servers are not reachable from the unit. It conflicts with
.B robodr\-spool\-export.service
(one consumer per spool). On a diode site this program runs on the SOC side
with
.B \-\-diode\-out
instead, from the SOC's own unit or procedure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-spool\-export (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1),
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
